The final deliverables provided to consortium executives comprise: (a) an asset-sharing operational contract establishing hub usage schedules, (b) a transparent financial transfer clearing matrix specifying scenario-wise cost responsibilities, and (c) verifiable Scope 3 carbon compliance reporting (
Z 2
) aligned with regulatory standards (e.g., EU CSDDD). In the event of an unforeseen disruption outside the pre-modeled scenario set S, the high computational efficiency of Level 2 EPML (0.32 s for 15 partners and 1.87 s for 30 partners, as reported in Table 8 allows managers to re-run the allocation model in real time. This rapid execution provides an algorithmic foundation for dynamic contract adjustments and automated smart-contract re-settlement during severe supply chain crises.
